# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Fatorati — committed PUBLIC browser configuration (production builds)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# These two values are public by design: Vite inlines them into the browser
# bundle of every deployment, and Supabase's publishable key is made to be
# exposed in clients (access is controlled by Row Level Security, not by
# hiding this key). Committing them here is what lets a build that runs
# somewhere with no dashboard variables configured — e.g. the Cloudflare
# Pages Git integration — produce a bundle that can actually sign users in,
# instead of failing with "Refusing to build a deployable bundle without
# Supabase".
#
# Precedence: a VITE_SUPABASE_* variable set in the real build environment
# (Cloudflare Pages → Settings → Variables and secrets, GitHub Actions
# vars/secrets, or an exported shell variable) overrides the values below,
# as does a git-ignored `.env.production.local` / `.env.local`. Rotate or
# move projects by editing this file, or by setting the dashboard variables.
#
# NEVER put a service_role key or an `sb_secret_...` key here (or in any
# VITE_* variable): it would ship to every visitor. See SECURITY.md.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://xithosetdfwoqbxmufvw.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=sb_publishable_r_lRnZ3zA6XVbi5uYJsHJg_ipF4eLnc
